itti","d":"2026-10-29T03:11:15+00:00","h":"tomgulittinhl.bsky.social","o":"NHL.com","t":"Flyers captain Sean Couturier after 5-2 loss to the Capitals dropped their record to 3-8-4 used the word \"soft\" to describe the team's physical play and battle level at times:","u":"https://bsky.app/profile/tomgulittinhl.bsky.social/post/3myyc67mzdsi3"},{"a":"Charlie O'Connor","d":"2026-10-29T02:25:23+00:00","h":"charlieoconn.bsky.social","o":"PHLY Sports","t":"Couturier: \"At times this year we're, you know, soft. I would say not hard on battles, and we lose battles easily. It's one thing to make mistakes and not win a battle. If you're in there trying hard and stuff, then it's different.\"","u":"https://bsky.app/profile/charlieoconn.bsky.social/post/3myy7m6ugnk2q"},{"a":"Tom Gulitti","d":"2026-10-29T01:29:41+00:00","h":"tomgulittinhl.bsky.social","o":"NHL.com","t":"Sean Couturier (10-1) and Christian Dvorak (10-3) are a combinded 20-4 on face-offs through two periods. The rest of the Flyers are 2-11.","u":"https://bsky.app/profile/tomgulittinhl.bsky.social/post/3myy4imdis2i3"},{"a":"Charlie O'Connor","d":"2026-10-29T00:40:32+00:00","h":"charlieoconn.bsky.social","o":"PHLY Sports","t":"Somehow, the Flyers have tied this game. Sean Couturier deflects a Nick Seeler point shot, and it eludes Thompson.\n\nIt does not feel like the Flyers should be tied in this game. But they are! 1-1.","u":"https://bsky.app/profile/charlieoconn.bsky.social/post/3myxzqq3ink2f"}],"team":"PHI","threads":[{"d":"2026-10-30T18:04:48+00:00","sub":"Flyers","t":"[O’Connor] Tocchet pushed back today on the idea that the Flyers' culture is going off the rails. He said he talked to Couturier about the \"soft\" comment (Tocchet pointed out that Couturier's critique was they were soft…","u":"https://www.reddit.com/r/Flyers/comments/1xjmopy/oconnor_tocchet_pushed_back_today_on_the_idea/"}],"videos":[{"d":"2026-10-29T03:52:11+00:00","id":"WfX-uftBuas","k":"presser","t":"10/28 PHI @ WSH Postgame: Sean Couturier",